Phase 4 (collaborative live view) + Phase 3 foundation (control endpoints). KEY ARCHITECTURE: agent and human share ONE device via the SAME /v1/android/* endpoints — an agent MCP tool call and a human's browser click both hit e.g. /v1/android/tap. So 'human steps in' needs no special handoff.

Endpoints (crates/xpressclaw-server/src/routes/android.rs, feature-gated, nested at /v1/android in server.rs): status, screenshot (image/png), dump, tap, tap-text, swipe, input-text, key. Each resolves the device target from the configured 'android' connector record (serial/tcp), default emulator-5554, then runs AndroidDevice (adb_client) inside spawn_blocking (adb_client is sync). Core AndroidDevice gained swipe/input_text/key_event (thin shell() wrappers).

Live view (frontend/src/routes/android/+page.svelte, sidebar link in +layout.svelte): polls /v1/android/screenshot ~1.4fps into an <img>, maps clicks to device coords via naturalWidth/Height -> /v1/android/tap, Back/Home/Recents -> /key, text input -> /input-text. MVP polling (no scrcpy); upgrade to scrcpy/WebRTC later if fps matters.

